      "findings": [
        {
          "id": "A1-RA-001",
          "severity": "blocking",
          "blockingAuthority": "author",
          "title": "Non-Windows timeout is marked re-entry-safe without proving descendant process-tree termination",
          "problem": "The approved A1 core-model spec requires that a fresh Full Test attempt MAY re-enter from `authorized` only when the prior child/process tree has been proven terminal. 013 implements owned whole-tree cancellation for Windows, but the unchanged non-Windows `runCommand()` timeout path sends SIGKILL only to the direct child PID and then returns `timed-out-cancelled` when that launcher closes. `runDeliveryFullTest()` treats `timed-out-cancelled` as a safe terminal transport failure, leaves raw status `authorized`, writes no executionBlock, and therefore permits an explicit later attempt. This proves only launcher termination, not descendant process-tree termination.",
          "contractRef": "openspec/changes/delivery-readiness-and-full-test-behavior/specs/flowkit-core-model/spec.md — `authorized crash 可 bounded re-entry`: only when prior child/process tree is proven terminal; transport-failure scenario: only process-proven-terminal failure MAY remain authorized for re-entry",
          "invariant": "Without a running/attempt ledger, every timeout path that leaves Full Test re-enterable at raw `authorized` must prove the entire owned prior process tree terminal. If whole-tree termination is not proven, Policy must fail closed and prohibit overlap rather than label the attempt safely cancelled.",
          "requiredOutcome": "Close non-Windows timeout ownership to the same invariant as Windows: either prove the owned descendant process tree terminal before returning a re-entry-safe cancellation outcome, or conservatively classify unproven termination as outcome-unknown and persist/block through the existing A1 executionBlock semantics. Keep the solution bounded; do not add a scheduler, running state, attempt ledger or background supervisor.",
          "acceptance": [
            "A real non-Windows descendant-survival fixture cannot produce re-entry-safe `timed-out-cancelled` while any descendant remains alive.",
            "Every timeout that leaves raw Full Test status `authorized` and permits later re-entry has a demonstrated whole-process-tree terminal proof.",
            "If non-Windows whole-tree termination cannot be proven, the attempt becomes fail-closed/non-reenterable through the existing outcome-unknown/executionBlock boundary rather than fabricated Verification failed.",
            "Windows taskkill whole-tree semantics remain green and unchanged in authority.",
            "Formal Change Verification selects and physically executes the new/updated timeout regression and remains passed on the revised exact candidate."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
